<title>PERU: Peru OKs two loans from Japan for debt plan.</title>
<headline>Peru OKs two loans from Japan for debt plan.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Peruvian government has approved two loans worth $118 million from Japan's Export- Import Bank to finance its Brady Plan to restructure foreign commercial debt.</p>
<p>According to a decree in Thursday's official daily El Peruano, the first loan for $38 million will be cancelled in 12 half-yearly quotas from September 2001.</p>
<p>The other loan for $80 million will be paid in 24 half- yearly quotes from October 15, 2002.</p>
<p>((-- Marco Aquino, Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134))</p>
</text>
